{%- comment -%}
  Renders a human-readable label for a variant option value or variant title.

  Part of this catalogue was imported with option values stored as
  percent-encoded slugs — "%e2%88%85-1114-mm" where a customer should read
  "∅ 1114 mm". The stored value is what Shopify matches variants on, so it
  cannot be rewritten from the theme; this only cleans up the text shown to
  the customer. Form values, input names and option-value ids keep the raw
  stored string.

  A value is only rewritten when it is *demonstrably* encoded: it contains a
  "%" and round-trips through url_decode to something different. Legitimate
  values pass through untouched — "6'7 - 130L" keeps its spaced hyphen,
  "50% carbon" keeps its percent sign.

  Output is unescaped, matching what it replaces ({{ value }}). Escape at the
  call site where the surrounding markup needs it.

  Accepts:
  - value: {String} raw option value, or a product_option_value / variant title

  Usage:
  {%- capture display_value %}{% render 'option-value-label', value: value %}{% endcapture -%}
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign ovl_raw = value | append: ''
  assign ovl_label = ovl_raw

  if ovl_raw contains '%'
    assign ovl_decoded = ovl_raw | url_decode
    if ovl_decoded != ovl_raw
      assign ovl_label = ovl_decoded | replace: '_', ' ' | replace: '-', ' ' | strip
    endif
  endif

  echo ovl_label
-%}
